  "canonical_short_name": "simple_line_graph",
  "relation": "the finite simple line graph on the edge-set subtype: Chromatic X43 x43_line_vertex/x43_line_rel/x43_line_graph and the Section SLine (Variable G) sline_rel/sline_graph of Reconstruction U11 and Minor containment are GTBase.simple_line_graphs.simple_line_vertex/simple_line_rel/simple_line_graph: the carrier {e : {set G} | e \\in E(G)} (X43's x43_edge_set unfolds to E(G)) and the relation (val e != val f) && (val e :&: val f != set0), in the same order, by conversion; each graph agrees pointwise with simple_line_graph and by the identity isomorphism. The six constructor proofs are related through the graphs they build (eq_diso), never by proof-field equality. Functoriality on isomorphisms (simple_line_graph_diso, promoted from Kelly) carries the identity isomorphisms through every iterate, zero included; the square's chromatic number moves along isomorphisms (chi_graph_power_diso). The pre-M1 carrier over the raw edge comprehension is another subtype of the same set, mapped by val. Hamilton U2's enum-ranked oriented-edge line graph is a deferred class of this family.",
  "baseline_commit": "897a7d30a0137195d30ae803d0482b5df31c3869",
