  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A25 (simple line graphs on edge-set subtypes), on the private prerequisite 2bec753 (A24 pin 897a7d3 plus four reviewed tool files, unchanged here). New GTBase.simple_line_graphs gives the iterable sgraph -> sgraph line graph on {e : {set G} | e \\in E(G)} with the relation (val e != val f) && (val e :&: val f != set0), its adjacency view and edge count, functoriality on isomorphisms (promoted from Kelly, whose LineDiso block keeps every name and type as thin wrappers), complete line graphs when any two edges meet, and the transport of graph powers and of their chromatic numbers. X43's three sources and the Section SLine of U11 and Minor containment (two each, the containment pair enrolled as public repository sources) are now aliases; the six constructor proofs are one-line uses of the public ones. The public client covers K0, K1 and three isolated vertices, K2, the three-vertex path, the triangle and the claw (non-injectivity), iteration and strong colouring.",
    "",
    "Frozen verbatim at 897a7d3: the seven sources, the six constructor proofs with their scripts (U11's and Minor's in dependency-ordered modules with the Section scaffolding), X43's strong edge colouring and six complete current Props (X43, X220's two rows, U11's Graham row, Kelly's Whitney inversion premise enrolled through additional_statements and implications_U11's external statement, both explicitly non-corpus and still conditional). Three complete Originals: X43 at 061154c on M1's raw edge comprehension and A1's raw induced-free, and both Whitney Props at A4's 9e03072 on A4's raw edge deck. Nine whole iffs, 36 mappings (20 current, 16 historical). The combined C19 X220 Original is coordinator-owned and not part of this pin.",
    "",
    "Proof consumers: Kelly's LineDiso block becomes wrappers with unchanged headers; Kelly's other proofs, grounding_U11, Minor sline_graph_card_gt0, X220's groundings and implications (e052 keeps both wall hypotheses), A1 and A4 certificates and Atlas implications_A1 recompile unchanged. Hamilton U2's four enum-ranked helpers are a deferred class with their bodies unchanged; GTBase.base's multigraph line_graph, X102's defective x102_line_graph_of and Infinite D4legacy's ordered-edge line graph stay distinct."
  ],
